  "title": "ERP paradigm of the Mobile BCI dataset",
  "description": "A mobile brain-computer interface dataset containing scalp- and ear-EEG recordings from 24 healthy participants performing a visual oddball (P300/ERP) paradigm while standing, walking, and running. EEG was recorded from 73 channels with additional EOG across five sessions per subject. This derivative version is formatted in BIDS with HED event annotations for benchmarking BCI decoding during locomotion.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded with a BrainAmp amplifier (Brain Products) using 73 Ag/AgCl electrodes referenced to FCz and grounded at Fpz, plus 4 EOG channels. Participants performed a visual oddball task with Target and NonTarget stimuli during standing, walking, and running. Data were sampled at 100 Hz, with impedance kept below 50 kOhm.",
